5. CONTRIBUTIONS
====================================================================

5.1 CONTRIBUTION FORK (LIMITED PERMISSION)

Notwithstanding Section 3(d), the Author grants You permission to fork the
official source repository and modify Your fork FOR THE SOLE PURPOSE of
preparing and submitting a pull request to the official repository. This
permission is subject to all of the following conditions:

  (a) the fork remains a recognizable fork of the official repository and
      keeps this LICENSE file, the copyright notices, and the Mod's identity
      (name, mod id, branding) unchanged;

  (b) You do not distribute, publish, advertise, or release any build
      (compiled or source) produced from Your fork to third parties — the
      fork is for development and review only;

  (c) You do not use the fork as the basis of a separate, competing, or
      rebranded project; and

  (d) once Your pull request is merged, closed, or abandoned, this permission
      covers no further use of the fork beyond keeping it as a historical
      record.

Any use of a fork outside these conditions is not licensed and falls back
under the restrictions of Section 3.

5.2 GRANT OVER YOUR CONTRIBUTION

If You submit a contribution (e.g. a pull request, patch, or code suggestion),
You grant the Author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, non-exclusive,
royalty-free, sublicensable and transferable license to use, reproduce,
modify, relicense, and distribute that contribution as part of the Mod under
this or any other license, without obligation of compensation or attribution.

You confirm that You are the author of the contribution, that You have the
right to grant that license, and that the contribution does not include
third-party code You are not entitled to submit.

You retain the copyright on Your own contribution. Submitting a contribution
grants You no ownership, co-authorship, or any other right over the Mod
itself.

